<onlyinclude>'''Organoid intelligence''' (OI) is an emerging biocomputing research program investigating whether laboratory-grown neural tissue, especially three-dimensional brain organoids, can serve as components of information-processing systems.

== Explanation ==
Scientists can deliver signals to neural tissue and record its responses using interfaces such as electrode arrays. A computer may interpret the recorded patterns to carry out a defined task. Research has demonstrated limited experimental tasks, but organoids are not miniature complete human brains, and task performance does not establish consciousness.

